WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:09.400
Once upon a time, there was a miser.

2
00:00:10.541 --> 00:00:13.683
The miser loved gold, but he hated to spend it.

3
00:00:14.903 --> 00:00:17.665
He just liked looking at it and keeping it for himself.

4
00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.088
One day the miser decided to bury his gold.

5
00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:25.910
He dug a big hole in his garden.

6
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.832
Then he carefully put his gold in the hole.

7
00:00:34.604 --> 00:00:36.965
"Gold, you are all mine!"

8
00:00:37.465 --> 00:00:38.286
the miser said.

9
00:00:38.306 --> 00:00:43.188
"No one except me knows where you are!"

10
00:00:44.488 --> 00:00:47.869
The miser laughed and did a funny dance.

11
00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.671
Every day the miser went back to his garden.

12
00:00:52.111 --> 00:00:55.673
He dug up his treasure and stared at the beautiful gold coins.

13
00:00:57.213 --> 00:00:59.134
He watched them shine in the sunlight.

14
00:01:01.295 --> 00:01:03.776
And every day the miser said the same thing.

15
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.824
"Gold, no one except me knows where you are!"

16
00:01:10.646 --> 00:01:14.509
Then he laughed and did a funny dance.

17
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.813
One day a thief was passing by the miser's garden.

18
00:01:19.134 --> 00:01:20.655
He heard the miser laughing.

19
00:01:20.675 --> 00:01:24.619
"Why is that miser so happy?"

20
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.101
the thief wondered.

21
00:01:27.722 --> 00:01:28.984
He peeked over the fence.

22
00:01:33.612 --> 00:01:42.494
He saw the miser hiding his gold, saying, "Gold, no one except me knows where you are!"

23
00:01:42.514 --> 00:01:47.676
"Now I know where your gold is too!"

24
00:01:48.336 --> 00:01:49.176
the thief thought.

25
00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:53.157
He grinned greedily and rubbed his hands together.

26
00:01:54.798 --> 00:01:57.799
That night the thief returned to the garden with a shovel.

27
00:01:59.839 --> 00:02:02.480
Quickly he dug up the gold and hurried off.

28
00:02:04.628 --> 00:02:06.989
The next day the miser went to his garden.

29
00:02:10.491 --> 00:02:13.613
He dug and dug in the ground but found no gold.

30
00:02:21.298 --> 00:02:23.299
No! This cannot be!"

31
00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:24.639
the miser shouted.

32
00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:27.341
"My gold is gone!"

33
00:02:29.542 --> 00:02:32.344
Several villagers heard the miser shouting, and came running.

34
00:02:33.424 --> 00:02:34.304
"What happened?"

35
00:02:34.704 --> 00:02:35.565
a woman asked.

36
00:02:35.585 --> 00:02:38.105
"My gold!

37
00:02:38.946 --> 00:02:42.166
Someone stole all my gold!"

38
00:02:42.867 --> 00:02:43.867
the miser cried.

39
00:02:43.887 --> 00:02:47.428
"Where was it?"

40
00:02:47.788 --> 00:02:48.688
the woman asked.

41
00:02:48.708 --> 00:02:53.449
"I buried it here in the garden," the miser explained.

42
00:02:53.469 --> 00:02:57.611
"Every day I dug it up and looked at it.

43
00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:02.732
And every day I put it right back in this hole."

44
00:03:06.316 --> 00:03:08.297
The villagers shook their heads sadly.

45
00:03:09.457 --> 00:03:11.498
They all knew the man was a miser.

46
00:03:12.979 --> 00:03:14.760
They all knew he loved gold.

47
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.582
"Did you ever take any gold out?"

48
00:03:20.082 --> 00:03:21.103
an old man asked.

49
00:03:21.123 --> 00:03:23.644
"Did you ever spend it?"

50
00:03:25.385 --> 00:03:25.945
"Oh no!

51
00:03:26.485 --> 00:03:29.627
I only came to look at it," the miser said.

52
00:03:29.647 --> 00:03:32.628
"Then I buried it again."

53
00:03:36.296 --> 00:03:39.599
"So?" The old man shrugged.

54
00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:44.644
"You can still come and look at this empty hole every day.

55
00:03:46.485 --> 00:03:48.347
You didn't spend your riches.

56
00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:53.252
That's the same thing as having no riches at all!"
